#
# security/egress-host.pf — macOS HOST-side egress firewall for isopod, the pf
# analog of security/egress-host.nft. Loaded with pfctl on the Mac (in a dedicated
# anchor), OUTSIDE the guest VM(s), so a box that escapes its container AND the
# guest VM still cannot flush it without root on macOS itself. This is the
# escape-resistant boundary the in-VM nft ruleset does NOT provide.
#
# NOTE: this file is rendered by render_tmpl (a bash heredoc), so it must contain
# NO backticks and no dollar-paren command substitutions — only the
# ISOPOD_PF_SUBNET variable (written bare below) is expanded.
#
# REQUIREMENT: boxes must be on a ROUTABLE vmnet subnet the Mac can see — i.e. a
# per-box VM runtime such as Apple container (github.com/apple/container, which
# gives each box its own VM + IP on a vmnet subnet) or a vmnet-based
# vfkit/krunkit/krunvm setup. It does NOT work with podman machine's default
# gvproxy user-mode networking (a box's traffic is host-originated, with no subnet
# for pf to scope). See docs/macos-host-egress.md.
#
# Rendered by "isopod egress apply" (the box vmnet subnet is substituted into
# $ISOPOD_PF_SUBNET) and loaded into the "com.isopod.egress" anchor.
#
# Per apple/container discussion #719, box-initiated flows are matched on the
# INBOUND direction with the box subnet as the source: the guest's packets arrive
# at the host on the vmnet interface as "in", and pf sees the box subnet as saddr
# (Apple container does not SNAT them away before pf's in evaluation).

# Private / link-local / metadata / CGNAT destinations a box may not reach.
# 169.254.169.254 is cloud metadata; 100.64/10 is CGNAT.
table <isopod_lan> const { 10/8, 172.16/12, 192.168/16, 169.254/16, 100.64/10 }

# 1. The box's OWN subnet (its gateway + same-subnet peers) must stay reachable,
#    or the box loses its default route / DNS. "quick" = first match wins, so this
#    precedes the LAN block below (the box subnet is itself inside 192.168/16).
pass  in quick inet from $ISOPOD_PF_SUBNET to $ISOPOD_PF_SUBNET

# 2. Box -> the real LAN / link-local / metadata / CGNAT: dropped. Your Mac keeps
#    its own LAN access (this matches only the box subnet as source).
block drop in quick inet from $ISOPOD_PF_SUBNET to <isopod_lan>

# 3. Everything else the box initiates (the public internet) is allowed, so
#    apt/pip/git keep working.
pass  in quick inet from $ISOPOD_PF_SUBNET to any keep state

# NOTE on IPv6: isopod runs boxes v4-only, and Apple container's vmnet is v4
# (e.g. 192.168.64.0/24), so there is no box v6 source subnet to scope a rule to
# (mixing inet6 with the v4 $ISOPOD_PF_SUBNET is a pfctl parse error). If a setup
# gives boxes a v6 subnet, add: block drop in quick inet6 from <box-v6-subnet> to any
